#### Stability Mechanisms

We incorporate two primary techniques to ensure training stability. First, the teacher θT\theta\_{T} is updated solely via EMA (Tarvainen & Valpola, [2017](https://arxiv.org/html/2605.02943v1#bib.bib26)): θT←α​θT+(1−α)​θS\theta\_{T}\leftarrow\alpha\theta\_{T}+(1-\alpha)\theta\_{S} with α=0.995\alpha{=}0.995. This update occurs every 5 steps to smoothly incorporate learned weights. A periodic hard-copy fallback (θT←θS\theta\_{T}\leftarrow\theta\_{S} every 30 steps) is applied on top of the continuous EMA to prevent excessive teacher-student divergence, ensuring the KL signal remains informative throughout training.

