###### Proposition E.3 (KL Boundedness under EMA).

Under EMA updates with per-step shift ‖Δ​θS‖≤ϵ\|\Delta\theta\_{S}\|\leq\epsilon and LL-Lipschitz KL, the steady-state divergence satisfies DKL​(πθS∥πθT)≤L​ϵ2/2​(1−α)2D\_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi\_{\theta\_{S}}\|\pi\_{\theta\_{T}})\leq L\epsilon^{2}/2(1-\alpha)^{2}, yielding continuous KL growth. In contrast, hard-copy updates produce sawtooth KL with peaks of L2​Tcopy2​ϵ2\frac{L}{2}T\_{\text{copy}}^{2}\epsilon^{2} and abrupt drops to zero, destroying the distillation gradient. (This bound follows from unrolling the EMA recurrence (Polyak & Juditsky, [1992](https://arxiv.org/html/2605.02943v1#bib.bib60)); we state it to explain the empirical contrast between EMA and periodic reset dynamics.)

